### IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client. The session lives in an HttpOnly cookie, so keep cookies enabled.
### The X-Requested-With header is required on state-changing requests that use the cookie.

@api = http://localhost:8080
@ai = http://localhost:5000

### AI service ------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{ai}}/health

###
GET {{ai}}/symptoms

###
POST {{ai}}/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symptoms": ["itching", "skin_rash", "nodal_skin_eruptions"] }

### Backend ---------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{api}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

{ "fullName": "Asha Rao", "email": "asha@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd123" }

###
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

{ "email": "asha@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd123" }

###
GET {{api}}/api/auth/me

###
POST {{api}}/api/predictions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

{ "symptoms": ["itching", "skin_rash", "nodal_skin_eruptions"] }

###
GET {{api}}/api/predictions/my?page=0&size=10&q=fungal

###
GET {{api}}/api/doctors

###
GET {{api}}/api/doctors/1/slots?date=2026-11-10

###
POST {{api}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

{ "doctorId": 1, "date": "2026-11-10", "time": "09:00" }

###
PATCH {{api}}/api/appointments/1/cancel
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

### Admin (log in as the admin first) ---------------------------------------
GET {{api}}/api/admin/dashboard

###
GET {{api}}/api/admin/analytics

###
PATCH {{api}}/api/admin/appointments/1/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

{ "status": "CONFIRMED" }
